19
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
I was pleasantly surprised at how well the narrative flowed from scout meeting to scout meeting,

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
touching on the author's experience,

21
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
And I reflected on my own troop while reading the book

22
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
And, while not yet a scout master, felt it prepared me to be a scout master,

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Learning that being the scout master is more than just knowing how to lead, but how to teach the scouts to lead.

24
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
I'd recommend this book to anyone.

25
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Well, thanks so much, Eric,

26
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I appreciate that

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
And, yes, So Far, So Good is definitely not a training manual.

28
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
It's not a step-by-step how to do things,

29
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
And here's the deal right.

30
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
This is why I wrote it the way that I did,

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Because how do you learn the kind of soft skills- I guess you would call them soft skills-

32
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
that a scout master needs are things that you really can't reduce to like step 1,, 2,, 3..

33
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
And you can't do in a training course or anything like that.

34
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
It's something that you have to work at, an experience,

35
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
And I had 30 years experience with it.

36
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
I felt like I got reasonably good at it

37
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
And after trying to get all this in writing to show somebody what I'm talking about,

38
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
the best form ended up being a story.

39
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Who knew?

40
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
But no, Eric, I really appreciate the review.

